course: dictionary
lesson: 8941
title: Silently and how things are done
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Silently is an adverb. An adverb tells you how something happens, and silently tells you that something happens without any sound, or without speaking. «Owls fly almost silently thanks to soft fringed feather edges.» The owl makes almost no noise as it flies, so silently describes the flying.
explain: When you meet silently in a text, look at the words around it for clues. «Fluent readers still use phonics, fast and silently» tells you that reading silently is reading in your head, with no voice. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «without making any sound» still makes sense, you have it.
explain: Sometimes the clue is what makes the sound, or what does not. «A hybrid car often drives silently at low speed in towns» tells you the car uses an electric motor at low speed, which is why it is quiet. The context gives you the reason for the silence.
fact: Silently is an adverb, so it tells how something is done.
fact: Silently means without making any sound, or without speaking.
fact: «Read silently» means read in your head, not aloud.
fact: «Owls fly almost silently» thanks to soft fringed feather edges.
fact: A hybrid car often drives silently at low speed in towns, using its electric motor.
exercise: «Owls fly almost silently thanks to soft fringed feather edges.» What does silently mean here? | Flying in a circle | *Without making any sound | Very fast and loud | Gently, while singing
exercise: In class, «read silently» means what? | Read aloud to the whole class | *Read in your head, not aloud | Read the book backwards | Read in a loud voice
exercise: «Fluent readers read fast and silently.» Which word is the adverb that tells how they read? | fluent | readers | phonics | *silently
test: «A hybrid car often drives silently at low speed in towns.» What does silently mean? | Very loudly, with the horn on | Quickly up a steep hill | Slowly and in pain | *Without making any sound
test: Mrs Hale says, «Please sit silently.» What does she want you to do? | Dance around the room | *Stay quiet and do not speak | Shout your answers across the room | Read the page out loud
exam: In «Cats jump at a cucumber placed silently behind them», what does silently tell us about the cucumber? | *It was placed without any sound, so the cat did not hear it | It was placed with a loud bang | It was placed by a cat | It was big and green
